{"code":"de","name":"German","native":"Deutsch","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A1","pronunciation":{"title":"Sound German from day one","rules":[{"rule":"W = V, V = F","explain":"German swaps them! WASSER = VAH-ser (water). VATER = FAH-ter (father). Read W as English V.","examples":[{"t":"Wasser","r":"VAH-ser","en":"water"},{"t":"Vater","r":"FAH-ter","en":"father"}]},{"rule":"Z = TS, S often = Z","explain":"ZEIT = tsite (time). SONNE = ZON-nuh (sun). Z always snaps TS; S hums Z before vowels.","examples":[{"t":"Zeit","r":"tsite","en":"time"},{"t":"Sonne","r":"ZON-nuh","en":"sun"}]},{"rule":"CH is throaty, EI = eye, IE = ee","explain":"BUCH = boohkh (book). MEIN = mine (my). LIEBE = LEE-buh (love). EI and IE are mirror sounds!","examples":[{"t":"mein","r":"mine","en":"my"},{"t":"Liebe","r":"LEE-buh","en":"love"}]},{"rule":"Umlauts ä ö ü change everything","explain":"Ä = eh, Ö = round O-say-E, Ü = tight lips EE. SCHON (already) vs SCHÖN (beautiful) — dots matter!","examples":[{"t":"schön","r":"shurn","en":"beautiful"},{"t":"Tür","r":"tewr","en":"door"}]},{"rule":"ß = sharp SS, stress the stem","explain":"STRAßE = SHTRAH-suh (street). Stress the verb stem: SPRE-chen, LER-nen. Endings whisper.","examples":[{"t":"Straße","r":"SHTRAH-suh","en":"street"},{"t":"sprechen","r":"SHPREH-khen","en":"to speak"}]}]},"alphabet":{"title":"The German alphabet: 26 + 4 extras","explain":"Same letters as English, new names — plus Ä Ö Ü and ß (Eszett). Spell names aloud: ICH HEIßE … (my name is …), DAS BUCHSTABIERT MAN … (that is spelled …).","letters":[{"t":"a","r":"ah","tip":"as in father: APFEL"},{"t":"b","r":"beh","tip":"same as English: BROT"},{"t":"c","r":"tseh","tip":"TS sound: CENT"},{"t":"d","r":"deh","tip":"same as English: DANK"},{"t":"e","r":"eh","tip":"as in bet: BETT"},{"t":"f","r":"eff","tip":"same as English: FRAU"},{"t":"g","r":"geh","tip":"hard G: GUT"},{"t":"h","r":"hah","tip":"breathy H: HAUS"},{"t":"i","r":"ee","tip":"as in machine: LIEBE"},{"t":"j","r":"yoht","tip":"Y sound: JA"},{"t":"k","r":"kah","tip":"same as English: KAFFEE"},{"t":"l","r":"ell","tip":"same as English: LAND"},{"t":"m","r":"emm","tip":"same as English: MILCH"},{"t":"n","r":"enn","tip":"same as English: NACHT"},{"t":"o","r":"oh","tip":"round O: BROT"},{"t":"p","r":"peh","tip":"same, less puff: PREIS"},{"t":"q","r":"koo","tip":"always QU = KV: QUELLE"},{"t":"r","r":"err","tip":"throaty or rolled: ROT"},{"t":"s","r":"ess","tip":"Z before vowels: SONNE"},{"t":"t","r":"teh","tip":"same as English: TAG"},{"t":"u","r":"oo","tip":"as in moon: GUT"},{"t":"v","r":"fow","tip":"sounds like F: VATER"},{"t":"w","r":"veh","tip":"sounds like V: WASSER"},{"t":"x","r":"eeks","tip":"KS: TAXI"},{"t":"y","r":"ewp-see-lohn","tip":"like Ü: TYP"},{"t":"z","r":"tsett","tip":"TS snap: ZEIT"},{"t":"ä","r":"eh","tip":"E with dots: MÄDCHEN"},{"t":"ö","r":"ur","tip":"round O, say E: SCHÖN"},{"t":"ü","r":"ew","tip":"tight lips EE: TÜR"},{"t":"ß","r":"ess-TSETT","tip":"sharp SS: STRAßE"}]},"counting":{"title":"Counting 0 to 100","explain":"Learn 0–12 by heart. 13–19 = unit + ZEHN (dreizehn). 20+ flips backwards: 21 = EINUNDZWANZIG (one-and-twenty!). 100 = HUNDERT.","numbers":[{"t":"null","r":"nool","en":"0"},{"t":"eins","r":"eyents","en":"1"},{"t":"zwei","r":"tsvy","en":"2"},{"t":"drei","r":"dry","en":"3"},{"t":"vier","r":"feer","en":"4"},{"t":"fünf","r":"fewnf","en":"5"},{"t":"sechs","r":"zeks","en":"6"},{"t":"sieben","r":"ZEE-ben","en":"7"},{"t":"acht","r":"ahkht","en":"8"},{"t":"neun","r":"noyn","en":"9"},{"t":"zehn","r":"tsehn","en":"10"},{"t":"elf","r":"elf","en":"11"},{"t":"zwölf","r":"tsvurlf","en":"12"},{"t":"dreizehn","r":"DRY-tsehn","en":"13"},{"t":"vierzehn","r":"FEER-tsehn","en":"14"},{"t":"fünfzehn","r":"FEWNf-tsehn","en":"15"},{"t":"sechzehn","r":"ZEKH-tsehn","en":"16"},{"t":"siebzehn","r":"ZEEP-tsehn","en":"17"},{"t":"achtzehn","r":"AHKH-tsehn","en":"18"},{"t":"neunzehn","r":"NOYN-tsehn","en":"19"},{"t":"zwanzig","r":"TSVAHN-tsikh","en":"20"},{"t":"dreißig","r":"DRY-sikh","en":"30"},{"t":"vierzig","r":"FEER-tsikh","en":"40"},{"t":"fünfzig","r":"FEWNF-tsikh","en":"50"},{"t":"sechzig","r":"ZEKH-tsikh","en":"60"},{"t":"siebzig","r":"ZEEP-tsikh","en":"70"},{"t":"achtzig","r":"AHKH-tsikh","en":"80"},{"t":"neunzig","r":"NOYN-tsikh","en":"90"},{"t":"hundert","r":"HOON-dert","en":"100"}],"rules":["13–19 glue unit + zehn: dreizehn (13), neunzehn (19).","21+ runs backwards: einundzwanzig (one-and-twenty = 21).","100 = (ein)hundert; 101 = hunderteins."]},"level":{"title":"Beginner: first words, family, food","goals":["Greet people and introduce yourself in German","Count, tell age, and talk about family","Order food and use basic present-tense verbs"],"units":[{"id":"A1-U1","title":"First words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U1-L1","title":"Hallo! Greetings and politeness","learn":"HALLO fits everyone. Mornings: GUTEN MORGEN. Daytime: GUTEN TAG. Evening: GUTEN ABEND. Leaving: TSCHÜSS. Magic trio: BITTE (please), DANKE (thanks), ENTSCHULDIGUNG (sorry).","vocab":[{"t":"hallo","r":"HAH-loh","en":"hello","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"guten Morgen","r":"GOO-ten MOHR-gen","en":"good morning","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"guten Tag","r":"GOO-ten tahk","en":"good day","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"guten Abend","r":"GOO-ten AH-bent","en":"good evening","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"tschüss","r":"chewss","en":"bye","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"bitte","r":"BIT-tuh","en":"please / you're welcome","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"danke","r":"DAHN-kuh","en":"thanks","pos":"noun"},{"t":"Entschuldigung","r":"ent-SHOOL-dee-goong","en":"sorry / excuse me","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Three genders: DER, DIE, DAS (ein/eine)","explain":"Masculine = DER/EIN, feminine = DIE/EINE, neuter = DAS/EIN. Learn every noun WITH its article: DER Apfel, DIE Milch, DAS Brot. Gender is part of the word!","pattern":"der/ein (m) · die/eine (f) · das/ein (n)","examples":[{"t":"der Apfel","r":"dehr AHP-fel","en":"the apple"},{"t":"die Milch","r":"dee meelkh","en":"the milk"},{"t":"das Brot","r":"dahss broht","en":"the bread"}],"mistakes":["Saying DIE Apfel — Apfel is masculine: DER Apfel.","Skipping articles — always DER/DIE/DAS or EIN/EINE."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Guten Tag! Wie geht es dir?","r":"GOO-ten tahk! vee gayt ess deer?","en":"Hello! How are you?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Danke, gut. Und dir?","r":"DAHN-kuh, goot. oont deer?","en":"Thanks, fine. And you?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Auch gut, danke. Tschüss!","r":"owkh goot, DAHN-kuh. chewss!","en":"Also fine, thanks. Bye!"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Tschüss!","r":"chewss!","en":"Bye!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: hello","answer":"hallo"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: thank you","answer":"danke"},{"type":"fill","q":"Guten ___ (morning)","answer":"Morgen"},{"type":"choose","q":"Which means 'please'?","options":["danke","bitte","hallo","tschüss"],"answer":"bitte"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Guten Tag, danke.","answer":"Guten Tag, danke."}],"quiz":[{"q":"GUTEN TAG is used…","options":["only mornings","in the daytime","only nights","never"],"answer":1,"why":"Tag = day: daytime hello."},{"q":"TSCHÜSS is…","options":["hello","bye","please","sorry"],"answer":1,"why":"Tschüss = bye."},{"q":"DER APFEL means…","options":["the milk","the apple","the bread","the door"],"answer":1,"why":"Apfel (masculine) = apple."},{"q":"Which is neuter?","options":["der Apfel","die Milch","das Brot","die Tür"],"answer":2,"why":"Das marks neuter nouns."},{"q":"ENTSCHULDIGUNG means…","options":["please","thanks","sorry","hello"],"answer":2,"why":"Entschuldigung = sorry/excuse me."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Greetings worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Match the greeting to its use.","items":["guten Morgen","guten Abend","tschüss"],"key":["good morning","good evening","bye"]},{"instruction":"Fill in: der, die, or das.","items":["___ Apfel","___ Milch","___ Brot"],"key":["der","die","das"]},{"instruction":"Write the magic words.","items":["please","thanks","sorry"],"key":["bitte","danke","Entschuldigung"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U1-L2","title":"Numbers and introductions","learn":"Numbers 1–10 open prices and ages. Introduce with SEIN (to be): ICH BIN = I am. Ask names: WIE HEIßT DU? (How are you called?). Answer: ICH HEIßE … Where from: WOHER KOMMST DU?","vocab":[{"t":"eins","r":"eyents","en":"one","pos":"number"},{"t":"zwei","r":"tsvy","en":"two","pos":"number"},{"t":"drei","r":"dry","en":"three","pos":"number"},{"t":"vier","r":"feer","en":"four","pos":"number"},{"t":"fünf","r":"fewnf","en":"five","pos":"number"},{"t":"sechs","r":"zeks","en":"six","pos":"number"},{"t":"sieben","r":"ZEE-ben","en":"seven","pos":"number"},{"t":"acht","r":"ahkht","en":"eight","pos":"number"},{"t":"neun","r":"noyn","en":"nine","pos":"number"},{"t":"zehn","r":"tsehn","en":"ten","pos":"number"}],"grammar":{"title":"SEIN: ich bin, du bist, er/sie ist","explain":"ICH BIN = I am, DU BIST = you are, ER/SIE IST = he/she is. German always keeps the pronoun — ICH BIN, never just BIN!","pattern":"ich bin · du bist · er/sie ist","examples":[{"t":"Ich bin Lena.","r":"eekh been LEH-nah.","en":"I am Lena."},{"t":"Bist du Max?","r":"bist doo mahx?","en":"Are you Max?"},{"t":"Sie ist Deutsche.","r":"zee ist DOY-chuh.","en":"She is German."}],"mistakes":["Dropping ICH (saying BIN Lena) — German needs ICH BIN.","Saying ER for a woman — she is SIE (lowercase sie!)."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Hallo, ich bin Lena. Wie heißt du?","r":"HAH-loh, eekh been LEH-nah. vee heyst doo?","en":"Hello, I am Lena. What is your name?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ich heiße Max. Woher kommst du?","r":"eekh HEY-suh mahx. VOH-hehr kohmst doo?","en":"My name is Max. Where are you from?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ich komme aus Berlin.","r":"eekh KOH-muh owss behr-LEEN.","en":"I come from Berlin."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Freut mich!","r":"froyt meekh!","en":"Nice to meet you!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am Lena","answer":"Ich bin Lena"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ du Max? (are)","answer":"Bist"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I am' in German is…","options":["ist","bist","bin (with ich)","sind"],"answer":"bin (with ich)"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: bin / ich / Lena","answer":"ich bin Lena"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich heiße Max.","answer":"Ich heiße Max."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH BIN means…","options":["you are","I am","he is","we are"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich bin = I am."},{"q":"How do you ask someone's name?","options":["Wie geht's?","Wie heißt du?","Woher kommst du?","Wie alt?"],"answer":1,"why":"Wie heißt du? = What are you called?"},{"q":"FÜNF is number…","options":["3","4","5","6"],"answer":2,"why":"eins zwei drei vier FÜNF."},{"q":"'I come from Berlin' is…","options":["Ich bin Berlin","Ich komme aus Berlin","Ich aus Berlin komme","Bin aus Berlin"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich komme AUS + place."},{"q":"FREUT MICH means…","options":["goodbye","nice to meet you","good luck","see you"],"answer":1,"why":"Say it when you first meet."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Numbers and names worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Write the numbers in German.","items":["2","5","10"],"key":["zwei","fünf","zehn"]},{"instruction":"Complete with bin, bist, or ist.","items":["Ich ___ Lena (I am)","___ du Max? (are you)","Sie ___ Deutsche (she is)"],"key":["bin","Bist","ist"]},{"instruction":"Introduce yourself in two lines.","items":["Say your name","Say where you are from"],"key":["Ich bin …","Ich komme aus …"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U2","title":"Daily life","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U2-L1","title":"Family and age (Jahre alt)","learn":"Meet the family: MUTTER, VATER, BRUDER, SCHWESTER. Age uses SEIN + JAHRE ALT: ICH BIN ZEHN JAHRE ALT = I am 10 years old. Ask: WIE ALT BIST DU? (How old are you?)","vocab":[{"t":"die Mutter","r":"dee MOOT-ter","en":"mother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Vater","r":"dehr FAH-ter","en":"father","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Bruder","r":"dehr BROO-der","en":"brother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Schwester","r":"dee SHVES-ter","en":"sister","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Sohn","r":"dehr zohn","en":"son","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Tochter","r":"dee TOHKH-ter","en":"daughter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Familie","r":"dee fah-MEE-lee-uh","en":"family","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Freund / die Freundin","r":"dehr froynt","en":"friend (m/f)","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Age: ich bin … Jahre alt","explain":"ICH BIN = I am, DU BIST, ER/SIE IST. Age: ICH BIN + number + JAHRE ALT. WIE ALT BIST DU? = How old are you? (German age uses SEIN, like English!)","pattern":"ich bin/du bist/er ist + number + Jahre alt","examples":[{"t":"Ich bin zehn Jahre alt.","r":"eekh been tsehn YAH-ruh ahlt.","en":"I am 10 years old."},{"t":"Wie alt bist du?","r":"vee ahlt bist doo?","en":"How old are you?"},{"t":"Meine Schwester ist sieben Jahre alt.","r":"MEY-nuh SHVES-ter ist ZEE-ben YAH-ruh ahlt.","en":"My sister is 7."}],"mistakes":["Saying ICH HABE zehn Jahre — German age uses BIN, not habe!","Forgetting ALT: JAHRE ALT travel together."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Hast du Geschwister?","r":"hahst doo guh-SHVIS-ter?","en":"Do you have siblings?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ja, ich habe einen Bruder und eine Schwester.","r":"yah, eekh HAH-buh EY-nen BROO-der oont EY-nuh SHVES-ter.","en":"Yes, I have one brother and one sister."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Wie alt ist deine Schwester?","r":"vee ahlt ist DEY-nuh SHVES-ter?","en":"How old is your sister?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Sie ist sieben Jahre alt.","r":"zee ist ZEE-ben YAH-ruh ahlt.","en":"She is seven."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am 10 years old","answer":"Ich bin zehn Jahre alt"},{"type":"fill","q":"Meine Schwester ___ sieben Jahre alt. (is)","answer":"ist"},{"type":"choose","q":"'How old are you?' is…","options":["Wie geht's?","Wie alt bist du?","Wie heißt du?","Woher kommst du?"],"answer":"Wie alt bist du?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: alt / Jahre / zehn / bin / ich","answer":"ich bin zehn Jahre alt"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich habe einen Bruder.","answer":"Ich habe einen Bruder."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH BIN ZEHN JAHRE ALT means…","options":["I have ten houses","I am ten years old","I like ten songs","I see ten birds"],"answer":1,"why":"Bin + Jahre alt = age."},{"q":"DIE SCHWESTER is…","options":["brother","sister","mother","daughter"],"answer":1,"why":"Schwester = sister."},{"q":"Which asks about age?","options":["Wie geht's?","Wie alt bist du?","Wo wohnst du?","Wie spät?"],"answer":1,"why":"Wie alt = how old."},{"q":"'My sister is 7' is…","options":["Meine Schwester ist sieben Jahre alt","Meine Schwester hat sieben","Meine Schwester sieben Jahre","Ich habe Schwester sieben"],"answer":0,"why":"Ist + number + Jahre alt."},{"q":"EINEN BRUDER UND EINE SCHWESTER means…","options":["two brothers","two sisters","a brother and a sister","no siblings"],"answer":2,"why":"Einen (m) / eine (f) = a. ."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Family worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["mother","brother","family"],"key":["die Mutter","der Bruder","die Familie"]},{"instruction":"Write the age sentence.","items":["I am 8 (years old)","My brother is 5"],"key":["Ich bin acht Jahre alt","Mein Bruder ist fünf Jahre alt"]},{"instruction":"Answer about yourself.","items":["Hast du Geschwister?","Wie alt bist du?"],"key":["Ja/Nein, (ich habe…)","Ich bin … Jahre alt"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U2-L2","title":"Food and present verbs","learn":"Food first! WASSER, BROT, MILCH, APFEL. Order with EINEN KAFFEE, BITTE (a coffee, please). Regular verbs: LERNEN → ICH LERNE, DU LERNST, ER LERNT. Drop -EN, add -E/-ST/-T!","vocab":[{"t":"das Wasser","r":"dahss VAH-ser","en":"water","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Brot","r":"dahss broht","en":"bread","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Milch","r":"dee meelkh","en":"milk","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Apfel","r":"dehr AHP-fel","en":"apple","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Reis","r":"dehr ryess","en":"rice","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Hähnchen","r":"dahss HEHN-khen","en":"chicken","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Kaffee","r":"dehr KAH-feh","en":"coffee","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Tee","r":"dehr teh","en":"tea","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Present verbs: ich lerne, du lernst, er lernt","explain":"Drop -EN, add -E (ich), -ST (du), -T (er/sie). LERNEN → lerne, lernst, lernt. SPRECHEN is wild (du SPRICHST) — regular verbs first, rebels later!","pattern":"stem + e/st/t","examples":[{"t":"Ich lerne Deutsch.","r":"eekh LEHR-nuh doytch.","en":"I learn German."},{"t":"Sprichst du Englisch?","r":"shpreekhst doo ENG-lish?","en":"Do you speak English?"},{"t":"Sie singt gut.","r":"zee zingkt goot.","en":"She sings well."}],"mistakes":["Saying DU LERNE — you needs -ST: DU LERNST.","Keeping -EN: ICH LERNE, not ICH LERNEN."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Guten Tag! Einen Kaffee, bitte.","r":"GOO-ten tahk! EY-nen KAH-feh, BIT-tuh.","en":"Hello! A coffee, please."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Groß oder klein?","r":"grohss OH-der klyen?","en":"Large or small?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Groß, danke. Wie viel kostet das?","r":"grohss, DAHN-kuh. vee feel KOHS-tet dahss?","en":"Large, thanks. How much is it?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Zwei Euro.","r":"tsvy oy-ROH.","en":"Two euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I learn German","answer":"Ich lerne Deutsch"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ du Englisch? (speak)","answer":"Sprichst"},{"type":"choose","q":"'A coffee, please' is…","options":["Ein Kaffee, bitte","Einen Kaffee, bitte","Einem Kaffee, bitte","Kaffee bitte ein"],"answer":"Einen Kaffee, bitte"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: Kaffee / bitte / einen","answer":"einen Kaffee, bitte"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Einen Tee, bitte.","answer":"Einen Tee, bitte."}],"quiz":[{"q":"DU LERNST means…","options":["I learn","you learn","he learns","they learn"],"answer":1,"why":"-ST = you."},{"q":"DAS HÄHNCHEN is…","options":["bread","rice","chicken","apple"],"answer":2,"why":"Hähnchen = chicken."},{"q":"WIE VIEL KOSTET DAS? means…","options":["Where is it?","How much is it?","What time is it?","Who is it?"],"answer":1,"why":"Wie viel = how much."},{"q":"'She sings well' is…","options":["Sie singe gut","Sie singt gut","Sie singst gut","Sie singen gut"],"answer":1,"why":"She = -T: singt."},{"q":"EINEN (not EIN) Kaffee because…","options":["coffee is plural","ordering uses accusative","it sounds nice","Kaffee is feminine"],"answer":1,"why":"Einen = masculine accusative. ."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Food worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["water","milk","apple"],"key":["das Wasser","die Milch","der Apfel"]},{"instruction":"Conjugate LERNEN.","items":["I learn","you learn","she learns"],"key":["ich lerne","du lernst","sie lernt"]},{"instruction":"Order politely in a café.","items":["a coffee, please","How much is it?"],"key":["Einen Kaffee, bitte","Wie viel kostet das?"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U3","title":"Describing words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U3-L1","title":"Colors and adjectives","learn":"Predicate adjectives never change: DAS AUTO IST ROT. But before a noun they add -E after der/die/das: DER ROTE APFEL, DIE WEIßE BLUSE, DAS KLEINE HAUS.","vocab":[{"t":"rot","r":"roht","en":"red","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"blau","r":"blow","en":"blue","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"grün","r":"grewn","en":"green","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"gelb","r":"gelp","en":"yellow","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"weiß","r":"vyess","en":"white","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"schwarz","r":"shvahrts","en":"black","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"groß","r":"grohss","en":"big","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"klein","r":"klyen","en":"small","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"Adjectives: plain after IST, +E before nouns","explain":"DAS AUTO IST ROT (plain!). DER ROTE APFEL (with -E). DIE WEIßE BLUSE. Rule of thumb: after IST = naked adjective; before a noun with der/die/das = add -E.","pattern":"ist + plain · der/die/das + adj-E + noun","examples":[{"t":"Das Auto ist rot.","r":"dahss OW-toh ist roht.","en":"The car is red."},{"t":"Der rote Apfel.","r":"dehr ROH-tuh AHP-fel.","en":"The red apple."},{"t":"Die weiße Bluse.","r":"dee VY-suh BLOO-zuh.","en":"The white blouse."}],"mistakes":["Saying DER ROT APFEL — before nouns add -E: DER ROTE.","Saying DAS AUTO IST ROTE — after IST stays plain: ROT."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ich mag das weiße Haus.","r":"eekh mahk dahss VY-suh hows.","en":"I like the white house."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Und das rote Auto?","r":"oont dahss ROH-tuh OW-toh?","en":"And the red car?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Es ist sehr schön.","r":"ess ist zehr shurn.","en":"It is very pretty."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ja, es ist groß und rot.","r":"yah, ess ist grohss oont roht.","en":"Yes, it is big and red."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: The car is red","answer":"Das Auto ist rot"},{"type":"fill","q":"Der ___ Apfel (red, before noun)","answer":"rote"},{"type":"choose","q":"'The white blouse' is…","options":["Die weiß Bluse","Die weiße Bluse","Das weiße Bluse","Die weißen Bluse"],"answer":"Die weiße Bluse"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: Haus / weiße / das","answer":"das weiße Haus"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich mag das weiße Haus.","answer":"Ich mag das weiße Haus."}],"quiz":[{"q":"DAS AUTO IST ROT: why plain ROT?","options":["cars are special","after IST adjectives stay plain","rot never changes","typo"],"answer":1,"why":"Predicate = no ending."},{"q":"DER ROTE APFEL: why ROTE?","options":["it sounds nice","before nouns add -E","plural","formal"],"answer":1,"why":"Attributive after der/die/das: -E."},{"q":"DIE WEIßE BLUSE means…","options":["the white house","the white blouse","the black blouse","the big blouse"],"answer":1,"why":"Bluse (f) + weiße."},{"q":"GROß means…","options":["small","big","red","fast"],"answer":1,"why":"Groß = big."},{"q":"After IST, KLEIN stays…","options":["kleine","klein","kleinen","kleinem"],"answer":1,"why":"Predicate adjectives: plain!"}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Colors worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["red","blue","small"],"key":["rot","blau","klein"]},{"instruction":"Plain or +E?","items":["Das Auto ist ___ (red)","Der ___ Apfel (red)","Die ___ Bluse (white)"],"key":["rot","rote","weiße"]},{"instruction":"Describe two things.","items":["The white house","The red car"],"key":["das weiße Haus","das rote Auto"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U3-L2","title":"Days, months, and telling time","learn":"Days are masculine: DER MONTAG. Time: WIE SPÄT IST ES? ES IST DREI UHR. Half past counts to the NEXT hour: HALB VIER = half to four = 3:30!","vocab":[{"t":"Montag","r":"MOHN-tahk","en":"Monday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"Dienstag","r":"DEEN-stahk","en":"Tuesday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"Mittwoch","r":"MIT-vokh","en":"Wednesday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"heute","r":"HOY-tuh","en":"today","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"morgen","r":"MOHR-gen","en":"tomorrow","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"gestern","r":"GES-tern","en":"yesterday","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"die Woche","r":"dee VOH-khuh","en":"week","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Uhr","r":"dee oor","en":"clock / o'clock","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Telling time: Es ist … Uhr + HALB","explain":"ES IST EIN UHR (1:00), ES IST DREI UHR (3:00). Half: HALB + next hour — HALB VIER = 3:30 (halfway to four!). Quarter: VIERTEL NACH DREI (3:15).","pattern":"es ist + number + Uhr · halb + next hour","examples":[{"t":"Es ist ein Uhr.","r":"ess ist eyen oor.","en":"It is one o'clock."},{"t":"Es ist drei Uhr.","r":"ess ist dry oor.","en":"It is three o'clock."},{"t":"Es ist halb vier.","r":"ess ist hahlp feer.","en":"It is half past three."}],"mistakes":["Saying HALB DREI for 3:30 — halb counts to the NEXT hour: HALB VIER!","Saying ES SIND drei Uhr — time is always ES IST."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Wie spät ist es?","r":"vee shpayt ist ess?","en":"What time is it?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Es ist halb vier.","r":"ess ist hahlp feer.","en":"It is half past three."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Sehen wir uns morgen?","r":"ZEH-en veer oonss MOHR-gen?","en":"Shall we meet tomorrow?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ja, am Dienstag um zehn Uhr.","r":"yah, ahm DEEN-stahk oom tsehn oor.","en":"Yes, Tuesday at ten."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It is three o'clock","answer":"Es ist drei Uhr"},{"type":"fill","q":"Es ist ___ vier. (half past three)","answer":"halb"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Half past three' is…","options":["Es ist halb drei","Es ist halb vier","Es ist drei halb","Es ist vier halb"],"answer":"Es ist halb vier"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: ist / spät / es / wie","answer":"wie spät ist es"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Es ist halb vier.","answer":"Es ist halb vier."}],"quiz":[{"q":"HALB VIER means…","options":["half past four","half past three","four halves","half a day"],"answer":1,"why":"Halb counts to the NEXT hour."},{"q":"WIE SPÄT IST ES? means…","options":["What day is it?","What time is it?","Where are you?","How are you?"],"answer":1,"why":"Spät = late/time."},{"q":"ES IST EIN UHR uses EIN because…","options":["one is lucky","Uhr is feminine (eine→ein?) no: ein Uhr is fixed","morning","all times"],"answer":1,"why":"Fixed phrase: EIN Uhr."},{"q":"German days are…","options":["lowercase","capitalised (all nouns!)","in English","never used"],"answer":1,"why":"ALL German nouns capitalise."},{"q":"MORGEN means…","options":["today","tomorrow","yesterday","morning only"],"answer":1,"why":"Morgen = tomorrow (also morning!)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Time worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["Monday","today","week"],"key":["Montag","heute","die Woche"]},{"instruction":"Write the time.","items":["1:00","3:00","3:30"],"key":["Es ist ein Uhr","Es ist drei Uhr","Es ist halb vier"]},{"instruction":"Make a plan.","items":["Shall we meet tomorrow?","Yes, Tuesday at ten"],"key":["Sehen wir uns morgen?","Ja, am Dienstag um zehn Uhr"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A1 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: hello","answer":"hallo"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am Lena","answer":"Ich bin Lena"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ich bin ___ Jahre alt (I am 9)","answer":"neun"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Do you speak English?'","options":["Sprichst du Englisch?","Spreche ich Englisch?","Spricht sie Englisch?","Sprechen Englisch?"],"answer":"Sprichst du Englisch?"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"Wie viel kostet das?","answer":"How much is it?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Der ___ Apfel (red)","answer":"rote"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: alt / bin / Jahre / zehn / ich","answer":"ich bin zehn Jahre alt"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Einen Kaffee, bitte.","answer":"Einen Kaffee, bitte."},{"type":"fill","q":"Es ist halb ___ (half past three)","answer":"vier"},{"type":"choose","q":"'My sister is 7'","options":["Meine Schwester ist sieben Jahre alt","Meine Schwester hat sieben","Meine Schwester sieben Jahre","Ich habe Schwester sieben"],"answer":"Meine Schwester ist sieben Jahre alt"}]}}}